# chromadb: three unpatched CVEs as of 2026-08-27, no fixed version exists for any of them —
# confirmed via upstream disclosure timeline (HiddenLayer reported since 2026-02, no vendor
# response as of the most recent public reporting). Cannot be resolved by a version bump.
#   - CVE-2026-45829 (Critical, CVSS 10.0): pre-auth code injection via trust_remote_code in the
#     collection-create endpoint. Only reachable if the FastAPI server is network-accessible.
#   - CVE-2026-45830 / CVE-2026-45831 (High): SimpleRBACAuthorizationProvider does not scope
#     permissions to tenant/database/collection; V1 endpoints bypass tenant scoping entirely.
# Mitigation (enforced in vector-db-launch/SKILL.md): the chroma server MUST bind to
# 127.0.0.1 only — never 0.0.0.0 or a publicly routable interface. Monitor upstream for a fix.
